-- R7 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md, extended by the review of
-- 2026-09-16: an action can pin only a value that can be COMPARED.
--
-- `g` names a function, so under R1 the action says "apply that exact
-- function" -- and matching an event against a pinned value is an equality
-- test, which two functions do not support. No event could ever match.
--
-- Until this was refused at check time the file checked clean and died at the
-- first trace with "trying to check equality on types that do not support
-- it", naming neither `g` nor the slot. Before R1 it was worse and quieter: a
-- bare name in an argument slot was a fresh placeholder, so the rule was
-- discharged by an event applying ANY function.
--
-- The EXACTLY spelling is refused the same way, because both spellings become
-- the same pinned pattern.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    apply HAS f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

GIVEN g IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`pins a function` MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST apply g WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH

GIVEN g IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`pins a function, the old spelling` MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST apply (EXACTLY g) WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH
